1. Shared DB (Anti-pattern)
Cons: Coupled DB tables, can cause lock down if one service fails

2. SAGA, where every microservice has it's own DB.
Overhead: Managing transactions that affect multiple rows in different tables.
Need for ACID (Atomticity, need to be able to roll back)

3. API Composition
Parent service leveraging other services through API's
CQRS: Command Query Responsibility Segregation a pattern that separates an application's write operations (commands) from its read operations (queries)
Pros: Scaling Read DB's and Write DB's horizontally very easily depending on load necessary
Cons: Ensuring Write DB replicates new data on view DB's on every update adding load to system

4. Event Sourcing
(Order cart for users)
Use Kafka to stream messages and trigger processes that update the view DB.
The view DB listens and reacts to events in the queue.